MODEL_FEEDBACK_JSON:
{
  "positive_alignment_reasons": [
    "The solder-seal connectors and liquid electrical tape felt useful because they address joining and insulating wires, closely connecting to my earlier crimp connector purchase.",
    "The outdoor Gorilla tape matched my repeated purchases of Gorilla tape and offered a clear use for patching and sealing repairs."
  ],
  "negative_misalignment_reasons": [
    "Neoprene cement and super-glue accelerator serve different repair needs from my vinyl cement; buying one adhesive does not mean I need supplies for other materials.",
    "The large heat-shrink tubing lacked a clear fit for my wiring needs, while the nuts, silicone oil, steel wool, and gallon of degreaser required specific jobs I had not indicated."
  ],
  "overgeneralized_signals": [
    "My repair purchases seemed to be treated as interest in almost any maintenance supply, even when I had no matching task.",
    "Similar purposes such as bonding or insulating seemed to count too heavily when material compatibility and dimensions could make the item unsuitable."
  ],
  "missing_or_underweighted_signals": [
    "My repeated Gorilla tape purchases give me a clearer reason to choose another practical tape than to try an unrelated repair chemical.",
    "I need a recognizable use and suitable specifications before choosing a supply; a broad connection to tools or repairs is not enough."
  ],
  "summary_diagnosis": "The recommendations understood my interest in practical repairs but stretched it beyond the specific tasks, materials, and sizes that would make an item useful to me."
}
